  "findings": [
    "Both caches retain every checked witness and fixed-work result. Reusing whole paths has most of the measured local benefit.",
    "All arms retain the outline-star failure; its missing edge fragment is diagnosed separately.",
    "The first baseline Viking repeats the original failed suite. Four cached runs pass, but no return-projection events occur during the relevant refinement. The baseline second repetition also passes. These outcomes cannot be attributed to the cache.",
    "The second fine-checker repeat increases error from 1.7075% to 1.841875% for both candidates. Strict no-regression is not established."
  ],
  "visualReview": "All 36 reconstructed images reviewed in the two contact sheets. The first baseline Viking has a visibly thicker/less complete curved silhouette; the other versions improve it. Fine-checker contacts remain uneven and vary across repetitions; several tiny seam/endpoint changes remain. Jigsaw, crown and bird differences are generally small. Review does not establish original cutting-path equivalence.",
  "decision": "Do not integrate either cache yet. Resolve timed candidate selection and retain the source/image-quality evidence before adopting a local speed optimization.",
